<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The rest ring, reforged: same concept as the original mark — a ring whose
    gap sits off-axis at 1:30 (so it is not the power symbol) with the dot
    seated in the gap; the between-sets moment, which is exactly when the
    phone is in the lifter's hand, doubling as a plate outline. The first cut
    (radius 24.76, stroke 8.49) read thin and cheap at launcher size next to
    the slab letterforms that dominate lifting apps, so the mass went up:
    radius 21, stroke 13, dot radius 7.5. The gap widened from 70deg to
    100deg (5deg to minus 95deg) so the fatter round caps and the bigger dot
    keep the same clear water — about 11deg a side — the thin mark had.

    Same two paths, same numbers, as `src/lib/assets/favicon.svg`: one mark,
    two renderers, no chance of them drifting. Centre (54,54); ring outer
    edge sits 27.5dp from centre, inside the 33dp radius Android guarantees
    is visible under every launcher mask. The glyph is white because the
    field (`ic_launcher_background`) is now the accent itself — app.css's
    white-on-blue-600 pair, 5.26:1 — where the favicon, sitting on no field
    of its own, keeps the cobalt glyph. The monochrome themed-icon layer in
    mipmap-anydpi-v26 reuses this drawable as an alpha mask, which is why the
    mark must stay a single-colour silhouette.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:pathData="M74.92,55.83 A21,21 0 1 1 52.17,33.08"
        android:strokeColor="#ffffff"
        android:strokeWidth="13"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M61.35,39.15 a7.5,7.5 0 1 0 15,0 a7.5,7.5 0 1 0 -15,0"
        android:fillColor="#ffffff" />
</vector>
